WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.433 --> 00:00:00.934
And Supreme

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:01.634
Court Justice

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:04.237
Samuel Alito is denying accusations

00:00:04.237 --> 00:00:05.605
that he leaked a Supreme Court

00:00:05.605 --> 00:00:06.973
decision before

00:00:06.973 --> 00:00:08.341
it was publicly announced.

00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:10.643
A former evangelical activist is claiming

00:00:10.643 --> 00:00:12.045
he knew about the outcome

00:00:12.045 --> 00:00:13.780
of a 2014 decision

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:14.647
before it was announced,

00:00:14.647 --> 00:00:16.416
according to the New York Times.

00:00:16.416 --> 00:00:17.450
In a letter to Chief

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:18.551
Justice John Roberts

00:00:18.551 --> 00:00:20.220
this summer that was originally obtained

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:21.287
by The Times.

00:00:21.287 --> 00:00:22.455
Reverend Rob

00:00:22.455 --> 00:00:24.924
Schneck says he was told by Gayle Wright,

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:26.359
a wealthy political donor,

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:27.460
about the discussion

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:29.963
involving a decision on contraception

00:00:30.196 --> 00:00:31.998
and the Affordable Health Care Act.

00:00:31.998 --> 00:00:33.299
The letter said Wright

00:00:33.299 --> 00:00:34.701
had dinner with Justice Samuel

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:36.536
Alito and his wife and claimed

00:00:36.536 --> 00:00:39.072
they spoke about the upcoming ruling.

00:00:39.072 --> 00:00:39.973
Now, CNN's

00:00:39.973 --> 00:00:42.008
Supreme Court reporter Ariane de Vogue

00:00:42.008 --> 00:00:43.176
joins us now.

00:00:43.176 --> 00:00:45.211
Arianna, I'm so glad you're here.

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:46.312
And the best Supreme Court

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:47.680
reporters in the country,

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:48.948
obviously, one of the biggest questions

00:00:48.948 --> 00:00:49.849
in Washington

00:00:49.849 --> 00:00:50.283
for the past

00:00:50.283 --> 00:00:51.551
several months has been

00:00:51.551 --> 00:00:53.820
who leaked the abortion decision.

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:55.655
But what do we know about this

00:00:55.655 --> 00:00:57.424
2014 decision?

00:00:57.424 --> 00:00:58.892
And what does this mean for the court

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:01.127
rival, as

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:02.629
you say, this man,

00:01:02.629 --> 00:01:04.230
the Reverend Rob Schenck.

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:06.399
He was an opponent of abortion.

00:01:06.399 --> 00:01:08.735
And at the time he ran this nonprofit

00:01:08.935 --> 00:01:10.570
and basically through donors,

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:12.572
he was trying to get access

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:14.340
to the Supreme Court justices.

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:16.242
And he said in this New York Times

00:01:16.242 --> 00:01:18.278
story that back in 2014

00:01:18.278 --> 00:01:20.480
he had one of his biggest donors

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:21.181
Gayle Wright

00:01:21.181 --> 00:01:22.482
she told him that she was going

00:01:22.482 --> 00:01:23.950
to have dinner with the Alito

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:25.952
she was going to ask about this important

00:01:25.952 --> 00:01:27.220
pending decision

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:28.755
and try to find out the outcome

00:01:28.755 --> 00:01:29.522
and he says that

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:31.057
she called him afterwards

00:01:31.057 --> 00:01:32.192
and basically said look

00:01:32.192 --> 00:01:33.793
Alito is going to write this

00:01:33.793 --> 00:01:36.629
and we're going to win this case.

00:01:36.896 --> 00:01:38.932
So flash forward a few years

00:01:38.932 --> 00:01:39.933
He, the Reverend Schenck,

00:01:39.933 --> 00:01:41.868
has now become a supporter

00:01:41.868 --> 00:01:43.203
of abortion rights. Right.

00:01:43.203 --> 00:01:44.504
And he learned that Chief Justice

00:01:44.504 --> 00:01:45.438
John Roberts

00:01:45.438 --> 00:01:46.573
last spring was going

00:01:46.573 --> 00:01:48.675
to launch this investigation into

00:01:48.675 --> 00:01:49.576
who leaked the

00:01:50.543 --> 00:01:52.078
decision overturning Roe.

00:01:52.078 --> 00:01:52.679
And he said, look,

00:01:52.679 --> 00:01:54.080
I have information

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:56.282
that could be interesting to you.

00:01:56.483 --> 00:01:57.083
It's worth

00:01:57.083 --> 00:01:57.684
noting, though,

00:01:57.684 --> 00:01:59.185
that Justice Alito

00:01:59.185 --> 00:02:00.386
issued a really strong

00:02:00.386 --> 00:02:01.488
and rare statement.

00:02:01.488 --> 00:02:03.523
They usually don't speak up.

00:02:03.523 --> 00:02:04.290
This is what he said

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:05.158
to The New York Times,

00:02:05.158 --> 00:02:06.159
and we obtained it, too.

00:02:06.159 --> 00:02:08.261
He said, I never detected any effort

00:02:08.261 --> 00:02:09.429
on the part of the rights

00:02:09.429 --> 00:02:10.096
to obtain

00:02:10.096 --> 00:02:12.165
confidential information or to influence

00:02:12.165 --> 00:02:13.566
anything that I did

00:02:13.566 --> 00:02:14.033
in either

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:15.735
an official or private capacity.

00:02:15.735 --> 00:02:17.737
And I would have strongly objected

00:02:17.737 --> 00:02:19.339
if they had done so.

00:02:19.339 --> 00:02:21.608
And I also talked to Wright yesterday,

00:02:21.741 --> 00:02:22.575
and she said that

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:25.111
the story was patently not true.

00:02:25.378 --> 00:02:25.812
But, Paul,

00:02:25.812 --> 00:02:26.746
you know what's interesting

00:02:26.746 --> 00:02:27.480
about this story,

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:29.215
it may not be so much about the leak

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:31.050
and whether it happened or not,

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:32.452
but that it really shows

00:02:32.452 --> 00:02:34.220
this behind the scenes effort

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:36.489
to try to influence the court.

00:02:36.489 --> 00:02:38.191
That feels really political

00:02:38.191 --> 00:02:40.493
and that really bothers the justices,

00:02:40.493 --> 00:02:42.562
because if the court begins

00:02:42.562 --> 00:02:44.631
to look like a political body,

00:02:45.165 --> 00:02:45.999
the fear is, is

00:02:45.999 --> 00:02:46.799
that the public

00:02:46.799 --> 00:02:49.135
is not going to take their decisions

00:02:49.135 --> 00:02:51.838
seriously. That's what's of real concern.

00:02:51.938 --> 00:02:54.073
And that might be the big import

00:02:54.073 --> 00:02:55.875
of this story, Paula.

00:02:55.875 --> 00:02:57.810
It's a great point Ari, on

00:02:57.810 --> 00:02:58.511
because this comes

00:02:58.511 --> 00:02:59.012
as public

00:02:59.012 --> 00:02:59.646
approval ratings

00:02:59.646 --> 00:03:01.681
for the court are at an all time low

00:03:01.881 --> 00:03:02.882
and a lot of questions,

00:03:02.882 --> 00:03:03.483
as you said,

00:03:03.483 --> 00:03:05.151
about political influence, questions

00:03:05.151 --> 00:03:06.519
about Justice Clarence Thomas,

00:03:06.519 --> 00:03:08.855
his wife's involvement in January six.

00:03:08.855 --> 00:03:09.055
I mean,

00:03:09.055 --> 00:03:10.823
how do you think that this will impact

00:03:10.823 --> 00:03:12.926
the public perception of the court?

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:14.294
Right.

00:03:14.294 --> 00:03:17.230
What we're seeing right now that

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:19.699
the polls show that the public

00:03:19.699 --> 00:03:21.401
is really questioning

00:03:21.401 --> 00:03:23.403
the legitimacy of the Supreme Court,

00:03:23.403 --> 00:03:25.104
and we're also seeing the justices

00:03:25.104 --> 00:03:26.406
themselves worried about it.

00:03:26.406 --> 00:03:27.140
Last summer,

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:28.341
we saw Elena Kagan

00:03:28.341 --> 00:03:29.976
give about three appearances,

00:03:29.976 --> 00:03:31.411
and she really talked

00:03:31.411 --> 00:03:33.913
publicly about that decision last term

00:03:33.913 --> 00:03:36.816
overturning Roe, a 50 year old precedent

00:03:37.217 --> 00:03:38.885
just because there'd been a change

00:03:38.885 --> 00:03:40.119
in the membership of the court.

00:03:40.119 --> 00:03:40.887
And she said, you know,

00:03:40.887 --> 00:03:42.622
when the court moves like that,

00:03:42.622 --> 00:03:43.756
it calls into question

00:03:43.756 --> 00:03:45.291
the legitimacy of the court.

00:03:45.291 --> 00:03:46.292
But interestingly,

00:03:46.292 --> 00:03:47.627
Chief Justice John Roberts,

00:03:47.627 --> 00:03:49.262
in his own public appearances

00:03:49.262 --> 00:03:50.463
and Samuel Alito,

00:03:50.463 --> 00:03:51.464
they really pushed back.

00:03:51.464 --> 00:03:52.999
They didn't name her,

00:03:52.999 --> 00:03:53.733
but they said, you know,

00:03:53.733 --> 00:03:54.701
you can't question

00:03:54.701 --> 00:03:56.369
the legitimacy of the court

00:03:56.369 --> 00:03:58.404
just because you don't like its opinions.

00:03:58.404 --> 00:04:00.340
So this is really bringing up

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:01.341
these issues

00:04:01.341 --> 00:04:02.475
that are concerning

00:04:02.475 --> 00:04:03.643
not only the country, but

00:04:03.643 --> 00:04:04.577
the court itself.

